# CSS Selector for Highlighted Paragraphs

```css
p.highlight {
    /* Your styles here */
}
```

## Explanation

This selector targets all `<p>` (paragraph) elements that have the class `highlight`:

- **`p`** — selects all paragraph elements
- **`.highlight`** — narrows down to elements with the class `highlight`
- **No space between `p` and `.highlight`** — means both conditions must be met on the same element

## Example Usage

```html
<p class="highlight">This paragraph will be selected.</p>
<p>This paragraph will NOT be selected.</p>
<div class="highlight">This div will NOT be selected.</div>
<p class="highlight important">This paragraph WILL be selected.</p>
```

```css
p.highlight {
    background-color: yellow;
    font-weight: bold;
    padding: 10px;
}
```

## Alternative Selectors

If you only want to select by class (regardless of element type):

```css
.highlight {
    /* Selects ANY element with class "highlight" */
}
```

For the fastest API build, here are your top options:

**FastAPI (Python)** - probably the quickest if you know Python
```python
pip install fastapi uvicorn
```
```python
from fastapi import FastAPI
app = FastAPI()

@app.get("/")
def read_root():
