Run: `uvicorn main:app --reload`

**Express (Node.js)** - super minimal
```bash
npm init -y && npm install express
```
```javascript
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.get('/', (req, res) => res.json({hello: 'world'}));
app.listen(3000);
```

**Hono (Node/Bun/Deno)** - even faster to set up, modern
```javascript
import { Hono } from 'hono';
const app = new Hono();
app.get('/', (c) => c.json({hello: 'world'}));
export default app;
```

**My pick**: FastAPI if you want auto-generated docs (Swagger UI comes free at `/docs`), Express if you already know JS.

